ro","id":179772110,"node_id":"U_kgDOCrcazg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179772110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero","html_url":"https://github.com/tciviero","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-01T20:27:37Z","updated_at":"2026-08-01T22:14:18Z","body":"Feedback addressed! The fix now works correctly with issue #94919.\r\n\r\nNote that the MRP in issue #97127 currently hits an unrelated segmentation fault, so it shouldn't be used for testing this PR directly (I've already discussed this with another maintainer and will open a separate issue for it). However, it still demonstrates the exact same underlying issue: local-to-scene causing material overrides to decay into sub-resources.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5153275535/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5153469596","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121983#issuecomment-5153469596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121983","id":5153469596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMyu0nA","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-01T21:14:52Z","updated_at":"2026-08-01T21:14:52Z","body":"Still can reproduce the issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5153469596/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5153900155","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121983#issuecomment-5153900155","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121983","id":5153900155,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMzJGew","user":{"login":"tciviero","id":179772110,"node_id":"U_kgDOCrcazg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179772110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero","html_url":"https://github.com/tciviero","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-01T23:04:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-01T23:08:20Z","body":"@YeldhamDev Sorry i hit close pull request by accident, could you please tell me the steps you took to reproduce issue #94919? Because i can not reproduce it with my fix.\r\n\r\nIssue #94919 reproducible without fix:\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa698751-b9a1-4be1-8d8c-af0cd54f8729\r\n\r\nIssue #94919 not reproducible with fix:\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/686d6204-1680-4d98-985e-87bff8fb9662\r\n\r\nThe MRP of issue #94919 is not a valid way to test the bug, as the `inheriting.tscn` scene has the material override already saved as a sub resource, so the path not showing is a sign that it is working as intended.\r\n\r\n```\r\ninheriting.tscn\r\n[gd_scene load_steps=3 format=3 uid=\"uid://br5scp8q5hlyv\"]\r\n\r\n[ext_resource type=\"PackedScene\" uid=\"uid://di86cgbqowsg3\" path=\"res://base.tscn\" id=\"1_e6uuj\"]\r\n\r\n[sub_resource type=\"StyleBoxFlat\" id=\"StyleBoxFlat_ligdb\"]\r\nresource_local_to_scene = true\r\n\r\n[node name=\"Panel\" instance=ExtResource(\"1_e6uuj\")]\r\ntheme_override_styles/panel = SubResource(\"StyleBoxFlat_ligdb\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nHere is the MRP which i used in the videos to demonstrate the fix\r\n\r\n[a.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30624328/a.zip)\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5153900155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5154007916","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121983#issuecomment-5154007916","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121983","id":5154007916,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMzPrbA","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-01T23:35:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-01T23:35:56Z","body":"From what I understood, the bug that #94919 reports is that if you remove that override, and then reopen the scene, the override will be present again.\r\n\r\nAnd actually, I think I found a regression in your PR: in the inherited scene, if I override that property with another `StyleBox`, then mark it as a `local_to_scene`, and then reopen it, the override is gone.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5154007916/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5154246463","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121983#issuecomment-5154246463","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121983","id":5154246463,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMzePPw","user":{"login":"tciviero","id":179772110,"node_id":"U_kgDOCrcazg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179772110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero","html_url":"https://github.com/tciviero","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-02T00:44:19Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T01:03:39Z","body":"If you are referring to the video I'm showing, that issue is not related to my pull request. Dragging and dropping a style and having it load as a built-in resource is a separate core bug. If I properly load it via the load button and follow your steps, the regression does not happen, confirming it is unrelated to my PR.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a001edf-6695-474c-8c83-12f179cc6c10\r\n\r\nRegarding issue #94919, I need to clarify a slight confusion regarding the technical terms used by the original author.\r\n\r\nThe core problem is that the user has 1 million child instances of a base grass scene using a grass material. When the scene gets instantiated (which happens everytime you open the scene in the editor) with \"Local to Scene\" set to `true` in the base grass material, every single grass instance material becomes an independent resource (a.k.a. a sub-resource, or an \"override\"), detaching itself from the base grass material in the editor. This forces the user to manually edit 1 million materials because they no longer reference the base one. With \"Local to Scene\", this behavior should only happen at runtime (allowing each grass instance to have a unique sway).\r\n\r\nWhat the author means by \"removing the override\" is that even if you manually re-add the path to the base grass material to turn the sub-resource back into an external resource (this can be done in the editor or by editing the scene file), reopening the scene causes the sub-resources to reappear. This happens because it is an instantiation bug.\r\n\r\nBecause this is an instantiation bug, the drag-and-drop behavior (which turns a flat material into a built-in resource rather than an external one) is a separate issue. It is unrelated to my fix and should be tracked and resolved in a separate pull request.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5154246463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5154395143","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121983#issuecomment-5154395143","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121983","id":5154395143,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMznUBw","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-02T01:20:24Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T01:20:24Z","body":"> If you are referring to the video I'm showing, that issue is not related to my pull request. Dragging and dropping a style and having it load as a built-in resource is a separate core bug. If I properly load it via the load button and follow your steps, the regression does not happen, confirming it is unrelated to my PR.\r\n\r\nNo, I'm talking about this:\r\n- In the inherited scene, create a new resource to replace the one in the `panel` property.\r\n- Mark that resource as local to the scene.\r\n- Save and and then reload the scene: the `panel` property reverts back to the original one.\r\n\r\n> What the author means by \"removing the override\" is that even if you manually re-add the path to the base grass material to turn the sub-resource back into an external resource (this can be done in the editor or by editing the scene file), reopening the scene causes the sub-resources to reappear. This happens because it is an instantiation bug.\r\n\r\nI don't think we are on the same page here. In the original MRP:\r\n- Revert the overridden `panel` property in the inherited scene, so it returns to its original value from the base scene.\r\n- Save and reload: that property shows as overridden again.\r\n\r\nUnless you're saying that this is a different bug entirely. If so, then this can be ignored.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5154395143/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5154483880","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121983#issuecomment-5154483880","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121983","id":5154483880,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMzsuqA","user":{"login":"tciviero","id":179772110,"node_id":"U_kgDOCrcazg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/179772110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero","html_url":"https://github.com/tciviero","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tciviero/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-02T01:42:40Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T02:03:10Z","body":"Now I understand, no, we were not on the same page. You are referring to a different bug; when trying to reproduce the issue, you found another one entirely.\r\n\r\nMy fix actually solves a specific instantiation issue: when you set the base material to be \"Local to Scene\" (Issue #94919), or the child as \"Editable Children\" and overriding the material (Issue #121428),  opening a scene with an instantiated child node causes its material to incorrectly turn into a sub-resource rather than staying an external resource (its path is empty rather than pointing to the base material), thereby losing its reference to it, this should only happen in run time (in the case of \"Local to Scene\"), in order to add a different sway to each grass, for example.\r\nIn one of the videos i posted it shows how my fix solved this and only this issue","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5154483880/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5154608037","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121983#issuecomment-5154608037","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121983","id":5154608037,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMz0TpQ","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://a